summary:
  Every budget reads as unlimited, so the ladder knocks at a dead station
  forever and the setting is decoration.

history:
  0 means "keep trying until it comes back" and had to stay reachable — the
  behaviour everyone had before the budget existed. That branch sits in
  front of the comparison that does the real work, which makes it the one
  line that can swallow the whole feature while every knock still looks
  correct: the intervals widen, the toast appears, the station is retried.
  The only visible difference is an hour later, which is precisely the
  complaint the budget was written to answer, so it would ship unnoticed.

target:
  package/contents/ui/RetryLogic.js

find:
    if (c <= 0) return true;

replace:
    if (c >= 0) return true;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_retrylogic.qml::test_the_budget_ends_the_knocking_after_its_last_round.
  Line-neutral.
